WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
So remember when, like Russia was meddling in&nbsp;
the American election and everyone was really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.840
afraid and it was this terrible thing? Turns&nbsp;
out that this is something that the U.S. has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:15.540
done forever. Like one of the things that the U.S.&nbsp;
has done a ton over the course of its history is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.160
throw out leaders in other countries that it&nbsp;
doesn't like or meddle in their elections or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.660
in their politics. That's what a coup is. And the&nbsp;
U.S. got really into this, especially during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:30.660
Cold War. They would send the CIA in to like&nbsp;
go foment protests and stuff and eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.720
oust the leader. Sometimes they would&nbsp;
like actually just like full on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.440
like assassinate the leader. It happened all over&nbsp;
the world, in fact I’ve been, like, deep in this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.300
trying to map all of the different coups, way too&nbsp;
many for me to cover. So I just settled on like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.460
17 of them that were particularly fascinating and&nbsp;
horrific. And I think after spending a lot of time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:51.780
thinking about coups, it was just a reminder&nbsp;
for me that we think we live in this world of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.800
like order and like there's rules and treaties&nbsp;
and all this stuff. But at the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.640
countries with the most power, they're&nbsp;
going to get their way no matter what.

